WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.550
Keys help us answer a basic question which row are
we talking

00:00:03.563 --> 00:00:09.093
about A primary key is the official row identifier
selected for

00:00:09.107 --> 00:00:13.464
a table A natural key comes from the business domain
such as

00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:19.148
a medical record number or national provider
identifier A surrogate

00:00:19.174 --> 00:00:23.545
key is generated by the database and has no business
meaning An

00:00:23.572 --> 00:00:27.835
alternate key is another candidate identifier that
still needs uniqueness even though

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:33.452
it is not the primary key A composite key uses
several columns

00:00:33.478 --> 00:00:39.551
together A foreign key references a key in another
table Do

00:00:39.578 --> 00:00:45.133
not think of all keys as interchangeable They solve
different problems identity

00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:51.092
business uniqueness and relationships As we continue
pay attention

00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:53.342
to which key is being used for each purpose
